  "ai_usage": "Drop-in site footer. Use it as the closing block of a marketing site, docs site, or app shell; it is deliberately generic so you can delete columns rather than invent them.\n\nStructure to keep: one <footer> landmark, each link group a <nav aria-label> containing a real heading, the newsletter input paired with a visually-hidden <label> (a placeholder is not a label — it vanishes on focus and many screen readers skip it), and the legal bar last.\n\nLayout gotcha worth copying exactly: the brand block and the link columns are TWO nested grids. If you put the brand in the same repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...)) row as the nav columns, the brand track absorbs the free space, auto-fit resolves to a single track, and every column stacks into one tall list. Keep .cols as its own grid so auto-fit only measures the columns.\n\nTune: --surface one step off your page background so the footer reads as a distinct region, --muted at or above 4.5:1 against it, and --accent for hover plus the button. Raise the minmax floor if your link labels are long, or columns will wrap mid-word.\n\nAvoid: burying the privacy/terms links (they must be reachable from every page), using placeholder text as the newsletter label, dropping muted text below 4.5:1 because 'it is only the footer' — that is the single most common contrast failure on a shipped site — and stuffing every route in here. Four columns of six links is the practical ceiling before it becomes a sitemap nobody reads.",
  "path": "effects/combos-recipes/site-footer.html",
  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Site Footer Block</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"site-footer\",\n    \"title\": \"Site Footer Block\",\n    \"summary\": \"A complete multi-column site footer — brand, link columns, newsletter capture, social row, and a legal bar.\",\n    \"description\": \"The block every site needs and no component library ships well. Four link columns and a brand block sit in an auto-fitting grid that collapses to a single column on narrow screens without a media query, a newsletter field pairs input and button on one row, and a legal bar carries copyright, locale, and the policy links that have to be one click from every page. Link hover uses a background-size underline sweep rather than text-decoration so it animates, and the whole block is one <footer> with real nav landmarks.\",\n    \"theme\": \"combos-recipes\",\n    \"categories\": [\"layout\", \"footer\", \"navigation\", \"block\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"footer\", \"site-footer\", \"columns\", \"newsletter\", \"links\", \"legal\", \"responsive\", \"grid\", \"auto-fit\", \"block\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\", \"html\"],\n    \"era\": \"timeless\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"beginner\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers. The link columns reflow on width via grid auto-fit + minmax with no JS; a single max-width query drops the brand above the columns on phones.\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"Static layout, no animation beyond link hover transitions on background-size. Nothing here triggers layout on interaction.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"Link groups are <nav> landmarks with aria-label so screen-reader users can skip between them, and each column heading is a real <h2> the groups are labelled by. The newsletter input has a visually-hidden <label> rather than a placeholder standing in for one. Muted link text is held at 4.5:1 against the footer surface — footers are where contrast most often quietly fails.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"--surface\", \"description\": \"Footer background — usually one step off the page background\", \"default\": \"#0f1219\" },\n      { \"name\": \"--muted\", \"description\": \"Link and body text colour; keep it at 4.5:1 on --surface\", \"default\": \"#98a0b4\" },\n      { \"name\": \"--accent\", \"description\": \"Hover colour and newsletter button fill\", \"default\": \"#7c5cff\" },\n      { \"name\": \"min column width\", \"description\": \"The minmax() floor on .cols that decides when link columns wrap\", \"default\": \"100px\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\n      \"Drop the newsletter row for a marketing-light or internal product\",\n      \"Add a locale/currency switcher to the legal bar\",\n      \"Collapse each column into a <details> accordion on mobile\",\n      \"Add a status-page indicator dot beside the brand\"\n    ],\n    \"related\": [\"glass-navbar\", \"hero-section\", \"pricing-card\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"Drop-in site footer. Use it as the closing block of a marketing site, docs site, or app shell; it is deliberately generic so you can delete columns rather than invent them.\\n\\nStructure to keep: one <footer> landmark, each link group a <nav aria-label> containing a real heading, the newsletter input paired with a visually-hidden <label> (a placeholder is not a label — it vanishes on focus and many screen readers skip it), and the legal bar last.\\n\\nLayout gotcha worth copying exactly: the brand block and the link columns are TWO nested grids. If you put the brand in the same repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...)) row as the nav columns, the brand track absorbs the free space, auto-fit resolves to a single track, and every column stacks into one tall list. Keep .cols as its own grid so auto-fit only measures the columns.\\n\\nTune: --surface one step off your page background so the footer reads as a distinct region, --muted at or above 4.5:1 against it, and --accent for hover plus the button. Raise the minmax floor if your link labels are long, or columns will wrap mid-word.\\n\\nAvoid: burying the privacy/terms links (they must be reachable from every page), using placeholder text as the newsletter label, dropping muted text below 4.5:1 because 'it is only the footer' — that is the single most common contrast failure on a shipped site — and stuffing every route in here. Four columns of six links is the practical ceiling before it becomes a sitemap nobody reads.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --page: #0b0d12;\n      --surface: #0f1219;\n      --line: #232838;\n      --text: #e7ebf3;\n      --muted: #98a0b4;\n      --accent: #7c5cff;\n      --radius: 10px;\n    }\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; }\n    body {\n      background: var(--page); color: var(--text);\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n      display: grid; align-content: center; padding: .8rem;\n    }\n    .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }\n\n    footer {\n      background: var(--surface);\n      border: 1px solid var(--line);\n      border-radius: var(--radius);\n      padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem 1rem;\n      font-size: .7rem; line-height: 1.6;\n    }\n    /* Brand and link-columns are two separate grids. Putting the nav tracks in\n       the same repeat(auto-fit) as the fixed brand track starves them: the\n       brand eats the free space, auto-fit resolves to one track, and every\n       column stacks. Nesting keeps auto-fit measuring only its own row. */\n    .top {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 1.35fr) 2.4fr;\n      gap: 1.4rem;\n      padding-bottom: 1.1rem;\n      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);\n    }\n    .cols {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px, 1fr));\n      gap: 1.2rem;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 460px) { .top { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }\n    .brand strong { display: block; font-size: .95rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin-bottom: .3rem; }\n    .brand p { margin: 0 0 .8rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 24ch; }\n\n    .news { display: flex; gap: .35rem; }\n    .news input {\n      flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; padding: .42rem .55rem;\n      background: #0b0e15; color: var(--text);\n      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 7px;\n      font: inherit;\n    }\n    .news input::placeholder { color: #5d6478; }\n    .news input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: transparent; }\n    .news button {\n      padding: .42rem .7rem; border: 0; border-radius: 7px;\n      background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font: inherit; font-weight: 600;\n      cursor: pointer; transition: filter .18s;\n    }\n    .news button:hover { filter: brightness(1.12); }\n\n    nav h2 {\n      font-size: .64rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .09em;\n      color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-weight: 600;\n    }\n    nav ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n    a {\n      color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none;\n      /* Animatable underline: a gradient sized from 0 to full width on hover. */\n      background: linear-gradient(currentColor, currentColor) 0 100% / 0 1px no-repeat;\n      transition: background-size .22s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1), color .22s;\n    }\n    a:hover, a:focus-visible { color: var(--text); background-size: 100% 1px; }\n    a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 2px; }\n\n    .bar {\n      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem 1rem;\n      align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\n      padding-top: .85rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .64rem;\n    }\n    .bar ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n    .social { display: flex; gap: .55rem; }\n    .social a {\n      width: 24px; height: 24px; display: grid; place-items: center;\n      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: none;\n      transition: border-color .2s, color .2s;\n    }\n    .social a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text); }\n    .social svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; fill: currentColor; }\n\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { a, .news button { transition: none; } }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <footer>\n    <div class=\"top\">\n      <div class=\"brand\">\n        <strong>Northwind</strong>\n        <p>Infrastructure for teams that ship on Fridays.</p>\n        <form class=\"news\" onsubmit=\"return false\">\n          <label class=\"sr\" for=\"nl\">Email address for the newsletter</label>\n          <input id=\"nl\" type=\"email\" placeholder=\"you@company.com\" autocomplete=\"email\" />\n          <button type=\"submit\">Subscribe</button>\n        </form>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"cols\">\n      <nav aria-labelledby=\"f-prod\">\n        <h2 id=\"f-prod\">Product</h2>\n        <ul>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Overview</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Pricing</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Changelog</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Roadmap</a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </nav>\n\n      <nav aria-labelledby=\"f-dev\">\n        <h2 id=\"f-dev\">Developers</h2>\n        <ul>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Documentation</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">API reference</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Status</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Open source</a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </nav>\n\n      <nav aria-labelledby=\"f-co\">\n        <h2 id=\"f-co\">Company</h2>\n        <ul>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">About</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Careers</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Blog</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#\">Contact</a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </nav>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"bar\">\n      <span>© 2026 Northwind Systems, Inc.</span>\n      <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"#\">Privacy</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"#\">Terms</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"#\">Security</a></li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"social\">\n        <a href=\"#\" aria-label=\"GitHub\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M8 0a8 8 0 0 0-2.5 15.6c.4.1.5-.2.5-.4v-1.4c-2.2.5-2.7-1-2.7-1-.4-.9-.9-1.2-.9-1.2-.7-.5.1-.5.1-.5.8.1 1.2.8 1.2.8.7 1.2 1.9.9 2.4.7 0-.5.3-.9.5-1.1-1.8-.2-3.6-.9-3.6-4 0-.9.3-1.6.8-2.1 0-.2-.3-1 .1-2.1 0 0 .7-.2 2.2.8a7.6 7.6 0 0 1 4 0c1.5-1 2.2-.8 2.2-.8.4 1.1.1 1.9.1 2.1.5.5.8 1.2.8 2.1 0 3.1-1.8 3.8-3.6 4 .3.3.5.8.5 1.6v2.2c0 .2.1.5.6.4A8 8 0 0 0 8 0z\"/></svg></a>\n        <a href=\"#\" aria-label=\"LinkedIn\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.6 5.3H.9V16h2.7V5.3zM2.2 0a1.6 1.6 0 1 0 0 3.1 1.6 1.6 0 0 0 0-3.1zM16 16h-2.7v-5.2c0-1.2 0-2.8-1.7-2.8s-2 1.4-2 2.7V16H6.9V5.3h2.6v1.5h.1c.4-.7 1.3-1.5 2.7-1.5 2.8 0 3.7 1.9 3.7 4.3V16z\"/></svg></a>\n        <a href=\"#\" aria-label=\"RSS feed\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 11a3 3 0 0 1 3 3H2v-3zm0-4.2a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 7.2 7.2H7A5 5 0 0 0 2 9V6.8zm0-4.3A11.5 11.5 0 0 1 13.5 14h-2.2A9.3 9.3 0 0 0 2 4.7V2.5z\"/></svg></a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
